WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.579
- I know my last business idea
didn't quite work out, but.

00:00:03.579 --> 00:00:04.995
- What was it again?

00:00:04.995 --> 00:00:06.580
- Beard oil for dogs.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.413
- Right.

00:00:07.413 --> 00:00:10.343
- I call it Groomio and
it's a guaranteed success.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.760
Turns out there wasn't much market demand

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.680
and the FDA called it unsafe and cruel.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.870
But my new idea is certain to take off.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.260
- Okay, let's hear it.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.710
- Coffee made from root vegetables.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.570
I'm calling it Beet Street Cafe.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.100
I've got everything planned out.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.900
I just need one person to give
me $200,000 to get started.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.520
- And where are you going
to find this person?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.380
- Oh, don't worry.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.213
They'll turnip.

00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:41.622
(upbeat music)

00:00:41.622 --> 00:00:44.372
(coins clanking)

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.680
Whether you're looking
to purchase inventory,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.490
expand your staff or
up your marketing game,

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.570
business loans can provide
the necessary cash flow.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.980
It's a pretty simple setup.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.190
You borrow a lump sum of money up front

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.890
and then pay it back
over time, with interest.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:02.930
Loans that are backed

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.250
by the US Small Business Administration

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.750
are the holy grail.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.920
Low rates, small down payments
and long repayment terms

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.970
are the norm,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.720
a winning combo for cash
strapped entrepreneurs.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.530
- But qualifying for an SBA
loan isn't always so simple.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.850
For starters, you'll
probably have to demonstrate

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.430
that your business has been
around for a couple years

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.140
and has a track record
of reliable revenue.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.760
- Wait, but doesn't
being a new business mean

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.880
that it's, you know, new?

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.010
- Yeah, it's kind of a catch 22.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.768
You have to be profitable
to qualify for funding,

00:01:35.768 --> 00:01:38.750
but most startups need
funding to be profitable.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.390
If you're just at the starting line

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:41.600
of launching a new business,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.240
a regular term loan might be a better fit.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.210
Interest rates are typically
higher than SBA loans

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.010
and your window to pay off your loan

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.640
will probably be smaller,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.760
but it isn't as hard to qualify.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.840
If that doesn't work out,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.060
you can look into a business credit card

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.730
to unlock immediate financing,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.310
but be ready to use your
personal credit to get approved.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.490
- That's a super important detail.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.520
Whether you're applying
for a business loan

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.560
or line of credit, lenders
want some reassurance

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.960
that you aren't going to
take their money and run.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.340
A strong credit score
essentially tells them

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.020
that you're good for it.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.960
Some lenders might even
require you put up collateral,

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.530
like your home or your car,

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.189
so that you've got some skin in the game.

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:22.940
Tread lightly.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.480
If you default on your payments,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.370
the repo man could come
knocking on your door.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.160
- Anyone who's ever watched an episode

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.090
of Shark Tank knows the setup.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.090
An entrepreneur pitches their idea

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.200
to a group of thirsty investors
who will hopefully bite

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.480
at the chance to get a
piece of their business.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.530
The winning shark then receives a slice

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.420
of equity in exchange for funding.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.610
This gives them an ownership
stake in the company.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:49.020
If the business does well,
they'll get a cut of the action.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.980
- It can be a win-win on both sides,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.710
but it's inherently risky for investors.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.060
If the business goes under,

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.970
the money they put in will
go down with the ship.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:58.950
It goes without saying

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.290
that you'll wanna craft
a killer business plan

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.750
and fine tune your sales pitch
before your pitch meeting.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.048
The question then comes
down to finding investors.

00:03:08.048 --> 00:03:08.881
(doorbell ringing)

00:03:08.881 --> 00:03:10.600
- There are a few ways to go about it.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.390
One option is to hit up friends

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.480
and family who want to get
in on your new business.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.770
But if you're denied a loan from the bank

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.420
of mom and dad, you can look

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.650
to an angel investor for guidance.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.260
These are individual investors
who usually have deep pockets

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.960
and a wealth of business experience.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.320
Most will come in and play an active role

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.310
in growing the company,

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.270
from doling out capital to
weighing in with business advice.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.310
- Venture capital is
cut from the same cloth,

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.000
but works a little differently.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.830
Instead of a single investor,

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.760
you're working with a
VC firm or fund manager

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.980
that's looking to drop large chunks

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.137
of cash into viable startups.

00:03:48.137 --> 00:03:50.370
The entrepreneur plants the seeds

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.150
with a great idea and solid business plan.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.070
Then VC investors water the
crops and watch them grow.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.048
- Crowdfunding can be
another way to pump cash

00:03:59.048 --> 00:04:00.990
into your new business.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.610
You can go about it by trading
ownership shares for capital,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.520
seeking good, old
fashioned donations online,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.447
or swapping products or
services in exchange for cash.

00:04:11.447 --> 00:04:13.060
Crowdfunding is pretty legit

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.576
and generates a lot of cash each year.

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:17.340
- This might sound kind of obvious,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.380
but you can also use your own money

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.720
to bring your business idea to life.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.740
Cash savings make for a
quick source of capital,

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.640
but be careful not to completely
drain your emergency fund.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.440
If your car breaks down or
your roof springs a leak,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.420
you'll need to crack open that
piggy bank to cover the bill.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.069
What we're getting at
here is that you always

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:39.170
wanna leave a little cushion
in your savings account.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.400
- A personal loan might make
for a better financing option.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.410
They are structured like business loans

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.270
and can unlock a one time pile of cash

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.430
that you can use for whatever
business expenses you want.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.870
One downside is that interest
rates are usually way steeper.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.410
You're also co-mingling
your business finances

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.800
with your personal credit,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.270
which will affect your credit
score for better or worse.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:05.020
- We've really only scratched
the tip of the iceberg

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.060
when it comes to business financing.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.960
Successfully funding your
idea really comes down

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.890
to your unique needs.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.950
A small team operation that
doesn't have much overhead,

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.819
probably won't need as much
cash as someone who's say,

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:20.070
opening a storefront business.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.060
- Your ownership stake
plays a big role too.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:26.270
While some entrepreneurs
are happy to give up equity

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:29.240
to get their hands on
some much needed capital,

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.150
others may be reluctant
to invite more cooks

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.220
into the kitchen.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.280
- This is all to say that
every business is different,

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.580
but understanding your financing options

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.658
is the first piece of the puzzle.

00:05:40.658 --> 00:05:44.220
And if anyone out there wants
to fund Beet Street Cafe,

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.839
that would be totally rad.

00:05:45.839 --> 00:05:46.683
- ish.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.690
- [Both] And that's our 2 cents.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.100
- Thanks to our patrons

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.820
for keeping Two Cents financially healthy.

